[2026-09-06T10:28:10.314Z] [8a2253e7-6195-4067-b209-1a69073a00d4] INFO REVIEW COMPLETE | iteration=1 | score=63 | rootCause=The render opens strongly, but the cut collapses into repeated process beats and then finishes with a generic plated CTA that never fully resolves the brand. The executable timeline also under-delivers on the promised commercial polish: typography is basic and oversized, the body section lingers too long on similar chef-hand shots, and the final brand cue is weak because there is no visible logo/signage. The result feels like a good sushi montage, not a premium finished ad. | issues=[{"severity":"HIGH","category":"PACING","timestamp_seconds":1.5,"problem":"The edit repeats the same roll-handling visual idea for too long before progressing to new information.","fix":"Cut the repeated middle hand-roll beats aggressively and move to the slice or plating beat sooner."},{"severity":"HIGH","category":"TYPOGRAPHY","timestamp_seconds":0,"problem":"The hook text is huge, generic, and feels template-like rather than premium. It dominates the frame instead of complementing it.","fix":"Use fewer words, smaller type, and tighter line breaks; favor one strong phrase like 'Fresh. Handcrafted. Precise.' with more breathing room."},{"severity":"MEDIUM","category":"CONTINUITY","timestamp_seconds":3,"problem":"The sequence jumps between similar kitchen angles without enough motivated progression, making the reel feel assembled rather than designed.","fix":"Order beats strictly by escalation: flame -> roll -> slice -> overhead plate -> hero -> bite -> CTA."},{"severity":"MEDIUM","category":"BRAND","timestamp_seconds":12,"problem":"The ending lacks a visible logo or unmistakable brand marker, so the CTA reads as generic sushi rather than KAIRO Sushi.","fix":"Keep the final frame on the cleanest plated dish and add a minimal location/brand lock-up that is smaller but clearer."},{"severity":"MEDIUM","category":"AUDIO","timestamp_seconds":0,"problem":"The commercial audio package does not feel fully finished; the SFX strategy is implied but not clearly impactful in the render.","fix":"Make the flame/slice/placement sounds more distinct and sync the final CTA hit to the last branded frame."},{"severity":"MEDIUM","category":"CTA","timestamp_seconds":11.8,"problem":"The call to action is understandable, but it arrives on a busy chef-plating shot rather than a true brand-end card moment.","fix":"End on the plated hero with the CTA text over clean negative space, not over active hands."}]
