[2026-09-06T10:51:33.308Z] [8a2253e7-6195-4067-b209-1a69073a00d4] INFO REVIEW COMPLETE | iteration=1 | score=68 | rootCause=The rendered Reel is materially shorter and less developed than the plan, and the actual execution does not reflect the intended premium commercial finish. It starts strong with an effective flame hook and readable typography, but then repeats the same rolling craft beat for too long, wastes runtime on a long, static sushi-prep segment, and never delivers the full branded finish promised by the plan. Audio execution is especially weak: the audit indicates only 2 SFX events and no visible evidence of the richer music/ducking/finished commercial sound design promised, while the CTA resolves into generic product coverage rather than a clearly branded invite. | issues=[{"severity":"HIGH","category":"PACING","timestamp_seconds":4.5,"problem":"The edit lingers too long on nearly the same sushi rolling/assembly visual, creating dead-air feel and reducing momentum.","fix":"Shorten the craft section to one concise proof beat; cut faster into a distinct next visual instead of holding one assembly shot across multiple seconds."},{"severity":"HIGH","category":"BRAND","timestamp_seconds":12.5,"problem":"The ending does not land as a clear branded CTA; it stays on product and chef hands without unmistakable KAIRO Sushi + Athens + tonight emphasis.","fix":"Finish on a cleaner, more deliberate brand-end card or food hold with explicit location/visit copy and stronger negative space for the CTA."},{"severity":"MEDIUM","category":"AUDIO","timestamp_seconds":0,"problem":"The rendered commercial does not visibly/audibly communicate the richer sound design promised by the plan; the audio feels under-finished relative to the visuals.","fix":"Add or rebalance premium music bed, tighten SFX placement, and ensure impact sounds and transitions are deliberately punctuating the cuts."},{"severity":"MEDIUM","category":"CONTINUITY","timestamp_seconds":2.5,"problem":"The opening hook and the following sushi-prep beats are too visually similar in tone and composition, making the transition feel repetitive rather than escalating.","fix":"Follow the hook with a clearly different angle or action beat to create contrast, then return to product detail later."},{"severity":"MEDIUM","category":"CTA","timestamp_seconds":13.5,"problem":"The final on-screen message is not instantly understood as a visit prompt; it reads like a product caption rather than an actionable invitation.","fix":"Rewrite the end text to explicitly say where to go and when: KAIRO Sushi, Athens. Come taste the difference tonight."}]
